onment 2408\n\n--- Record 2443 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Exposing APIs via UCL\nDescription: You can now expose APIs via UCL (Unified Customer Landscape) for the usage in BAS (SAP Business Application Studio) and SAP Build. You can do this by creating packages and assigning them to the required APIs in ABAP development tools for Eclipse.  For more information, see Working with API Packages.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-09\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2444 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Improved CDS Buffering - Buffer Propagation\nDescription: Extend the reach of the CDS/ABAP buffering approach and optimize the memory consumption with buffer propagation to enable the ASQL runtime to read denormalized elements within CDS view entities directly from the ABAP buffer instead of pushing the joins to the database.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-08-16\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2445 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Maintain Business Roles\nDescription: The Mass Change Wizard has been expanded so that you can also use it for derived business roles.  For more information, see Maintain Business Roles.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-09\nValid as Of: 2024-08-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2408\n\n--- Record 2446 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: OData API: Support User - Read Integration\nDescription: The following API is now available to retrieve support user data:  Support User – Read Integration  The following corresponding communication scenario is available:  Support User Request Log Integration (SAP_COM_0347) 