vely uses SAP HANA federation capabilities (taking advantage of SAP HANA Smart Data Access). In this new dynamic access, you can model external data sources using the new CDS external entities and the new logical external schemas. The CDS external entities can\",516\n802,\"--- Record 2911 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Field Extension Wizard\nDescription: You can now use the field extension wizard in ABAP development tools for Eclipse to create extension fields.  For more information, see Generating Extension Fields.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2912 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Hello, ABAP Cloud! Page\nDescription: Are you wondering where to find information about ABAP Cloud like documentation, release notes, roadmap or where to find examples with different levels of complexity complexity? The ABAP Cloud landing page in the ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse shows all of this information and helps to find everything about ABAP Cloud in one place.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2913 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: IAM Information System\nDescription: With this feature you can display whether a dependent business catalog is optional. You can view this information on the Business Catalog -Dependent Business Catalog tab. You can also display the related spaces and pages for a business role.  For more information, see IAM Information System.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-26\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2914 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Maintain Business Roles\nDescription: With this feature you define several general restrictions as leading. You can do this by selecting the required restrictions and then clicking Leading. In addition to this, you can now also filter for undefined restrictions in the Maintain Restrictions UI.  For more information, see Maintain Business Roles.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-26\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2915 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Maintain SAML 2.0 Configuration\nDescription: With this feature you can now upload the primary and secondary signing certificates you have maintained within the Cloud Identity Services.  For more information, see Maintain SAML 2.0 Configuration.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-26\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2916 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Maintain Translations\nDescription: New CDS annotations are now supported for translation: UI.dataPoint.title, EnterpriseSearch.modelName and EnterpriseSearch.modelNamePlural in data definitions and metadata extensions.  For more information, see CDS-Based Enterprise Search Models.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2917 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: New Transport Option in the ABAP Repository Wizard\nDescription: The new transport option Manual with preselection is now the default option when a maintenance object is generated using the Generate ABAP Repository Objects wizard. See Generating a Business Configuration Maintenance Object with the Generate ABAP Repository Objects Wizard\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2918 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Result Cardinality for Factory Actions\nDescription: You can now define the result cardinality [1..*] for factory actions.  For more information on actions, see Actions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2919 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: SAP Fiori Launchpad: Manage Pages and Spaces\nDescription: You can now merge your spaces or pages at the same time that you create or copy a new space or a new page in the Manage Launchpad Spaces and Manage Launchpad Pages apps. Previously, you had to do this in a separate step but now you can add the merge ID directly. In addition, the value help now also shows predefined spaces or pages, for example, as delivered by SAP.  For more information, see Merging Pages and Merging Spaces.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-17\nValid as Of: 2024-05-17\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2405\n\n--- Record 2920 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: SAP Fiori Launchpad: User Names in Manage Views Dialog\nDescription:\",414\n367,\"Type: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-09-03\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 287 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Referenced SAPUI5 Version\nDescription: As part of hotfix collection 4 (which is used for the standard upgrade), SAPUI5 version 1.136.4 is used for the administrator’s SAP Fiori launchpad, SAP-delivered Fiori apps, and the custom-built SAP Fiori apps, which are deployed to the ABAP system.  See SAP BTP ABAP Environment – Maintenance Windows and Major Upgrade Windows in 2025 and SAP UI5\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-15\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 288 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: SAP Fiori Launchpad: Manage Launchpad Spaces and Pages: Redesign and Renaming\nDescription: In the SAP Fiori launchpad, both the Manage Launchpad Spaces and Manage Launchpad Pages apps were redesigned. We adapted the overview pages to enhance working with spaces and space templates, as well as with pages and page templates. \"\"Predefined\"\" and \"\"SAP-Delivered\"\" were renamed to \"\"Templates\"\" to ensure consistent terminology between these apps, the Maintain Business Roles app and the ABAP Development Tools for space and page templates.  See Manage Launchpad Spaces and Manage Launchpad Pages.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-25\nValid as Of: 2025-08-15\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 289 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: SAP Fiori Launchpad: New Layout for Launchpad Shell Bar and Menus\nDescription: The layout of the SAP Fiori launchpad shell bar, user menu, notifications list, navigation menu and user settings was changed according to the current SAP Design System. The user experience was harmonized across different SAP products. The navigation menu was enhanced and is now part of the shell bar. It now offers access to My Home, Favorite Apps, My Spaces and All Spaces.   The sorting options in the notifications list were simplified. In addition, there is a new button to directly open the settings from here. The order of entries in the user menu as well as in the user settings has been adapted.  See User Menu, Shell and Shell Bar and Working with